<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605201212-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605201212-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202605201212-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605201212-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Contribution to the 4th workshop of the measurement & computation of fire phenomena (macfp) working group of the international association for fire safety science: experimental data".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605201212-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "As a contribution to the 4th Workshop of the Measurement & Computation of Fire Phenomena (MaCFP) Working Group of the International Association for Fire Safety Science (IAFSS), the Institute of Building Materials, Concrete Construction and Fire Safety (iBMB) at Technische Universität Braunschweig generated a comprehensive experimental dataset. The dataset comprises results from thermogravimetric analysis (TGA), microscale combustion calorimetry (MCC) and cone calorimetry under both open and controlled atmosphere conditions. The key experimental parameters and experimental conditions are documented in the accompanying README file.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605201212-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605201212-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605201212-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605201212-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605201212-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202605201212-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605201212-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605201212-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605201212-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403130624-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403130624-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202403130624-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403130624-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Database of recorded serial manufactured mlk-buildings (gdr) (release 2)".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403130624-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Lightweight construction in structural engineering meets the principles of contemporary requirements for resource-efficient design and has already established itself as a building block for sustainable management in the construction industry of the high modernism. However, little is known about the planning, execution and sale of marketable lightweight metal structures, which were developed in parallel in the GDR and the Federal Republic of Germany under disparate conditions from the end of the 1960s onwards. The \\'VEB Metalleichtbaukombinat\\' (MLK), a association of enterprises of structural steel engineering in the GDR, represents an association of constructive steel construction companies in the GDR in the years 1969 to 1990. In order to record and classify the serial manufactured buildings from the years 1969 to 1989, it is necessary to evaluate corresponding archival records, interviews with contemporary witnesses and material investigations, which provide the basis for a critical assessment of serial manufactured buildings built and still standing today. In the subsequent analysis from an industrial archaeological perspective, existing serial manufactured MLK buildings will be viewed from the perspective of monument conservation. Specific characteristics of individual systems can be derived from hall structures, such as the centre distances of the frames, the skylights and the roof pitch and shape given via the supporting structure. These represent the attributes for the manual as well as for the systematic evaluation of aerial photographs. For this purpose, the approach of deep learning, a special method of machine learning, is used to automatically record such structures. Submission of additional locations is encouraged via Email. Publication of the data will make use of revisions, released irregularly. The focus of the locations is on serially manufactured steel buildings with lattice construction, but the buildings may also be useful without serial features or with solid wall beams. The content is a compilation of recorded locations of the \\'Typ Ruhland\\' rod network and the \\'KT60L\\' sports hall extension of the MKL (GDR). Release 2 adds more locations for these two building types. In addition, coordinates for the sports hall types \\'GT60L\\' or \\'GT120L\\' and \\'42x24\\' or \\'24x42\\' have been added. These hall types contain the room structure \\'Type Weimar\\' (GT) or the rod net folding system \\'Type Berlin\\' (42x24).".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403130624-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403130624-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403130624-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2024"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403130624-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403130624-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202403130624-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403130624-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403130624-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403130624-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506031524-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506031524-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202506031524-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506031524-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Structural testing data of shotcrete 3d printed (sc3dp) and cast reinforced concrete beams: four-point and three-point bending testing results, including digital image correlation and distributed fibre optics measurements".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506031524-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset was produced as a result of structural testing of full-scale reinforced concrete beams of two types, with the same external dimensions but different reinforcement layout reflecting fabrication methods. One type was traditionally cast, and features modern orthogonal reinforcement composed of longitudinal bars and stirrups. The other type was digitally fabricated with Shotcrete 3D Printing (SC3DP) additive manufacturing method, and with force-flow aligned reinforcement in form of bent-up steel reinforcement bars. Both types were tested under three- and four-point bending, to investigate their response under shear force and bending moment respectively. The results encompass 1. Deflection of beam vs applied external load; 2. Crack opening obtained with Digital Image Correlation during test, and 3. Strain profiles along reinforcement bars of SC3DP testing beam. The data is time synchronised with frequency of 1/8Hz.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506031524-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506031524-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506031524-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2025"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506031524-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506031524-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202506031524-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506031524-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506031524-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506031524-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404191428-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404191428-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202404191428-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404191428-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "A system dynamics air transport system simulation model to test transition pathways".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404191428-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This collection contains a system dynamics model of the air transport system (ATS), developed to assess the different aviation environmental emission reduction strategies using the adoption of hydrogen-electric, hydrogen combustion and SAF. The model consists of the interaction between four major segments, namely air travel demand, airline industry, fuel producers and aircraft manufacturers. The provided files can be executed using the software Vensim. Furthermore, two data sets as an Excel file, containing a collection of initial values, parameters, exogenous variables and variables used to calibrate the ATS model are given.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404191428-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404191428-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404191428-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2024"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404191428-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
