<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202401090827-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202401090827-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202401090827-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "MIT-License".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151156-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151156-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202403151156-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151156-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Elpaso acmore - python module for faster training and evaluation of vibroacoustic systems with model order reduction".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151156-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The dataset contains the software publication artifacts for the software \\'elPaSo AcMoRe - Python module for faster training and evaluation of vibroacoustic systems with model order reduction\\' versioned 24.03.4. AcMoRe provides a wide range of functionalities to generate surrogates in frequency and parameter domains for vibroacoustic problems. As a result, one can benefit from faster computations by replacing expensive direct solvers with the yielded reduced-order model (ROM). In addition, to the compute capabilities, the tool offers various visualization routines that enable better insights into the ROM modeling process. The executions are performed in tandem with the elPaSo Research module for the offline ROM creation phase.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151156-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151156-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151156-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2024"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151156-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151156-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202403151156-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151156-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151156-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151156-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "GNU-Lesser-GPL-v3.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071056-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071056-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202510071056-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071056-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Microeit simulation images (electric sight)".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071056-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This data provide here as supplementary information shows the image results of image reconstruction using traditional imaging methods (GN, TV) and our trained machine learning models during the development and testing of the 1D-CNN model for the microEIT system. Groundtruch, CNN images trained with different SNR datasets, CNN images trained with 33dB but load with different SNR dataset, GN images load with different SNR dataset and TV images load with different SNR dataset are also provided. Image reconstruction results obtained using our 1D-CNN show significant advantages over the two traditional methods. This was replicated for two common excitation/measurement modes and was extended to objects with different conductivity and of varying quantities.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071056-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071056-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071056-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2025"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071056-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071056-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202510071056-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071056-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071056-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071056-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202411191155-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202411191155-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202411191155-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202411191155-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Bed shear stress measurements in rough beds flows through sparse array of rigid emergent vegetation".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202411191155-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset provides the hydraulic boundary conditions, bed shear stress measurements, and double-averaged velocity measurements collected in flume experiments presented in the article \\'Bed shear stress model for rough bed flows through rigid emergent vegetation\\' (Aliaga & Aberle, 2025). This research characterizes bed shear stress and double-averaged flow characteristics in rough-bed flows covered with sparse arrays of rigid emergent cylinders. For this purpose, a novel adaptation of a shear plate was used to directly measure the bed shear stress acting at the canopy scale. These bed shear stress measurements were analyzed in relation to spatially averaged near-bed flow quantities for two array densities and a reference scenario without cylinders. The primary outcome of this research is the formulation of a bed shear stress model for rough-bed flows covered with rigid emergent vegetation.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202411191155-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202411191155-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202411191155-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2025"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202411191155-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202411191155-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202411191155-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202411191155-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202411191155-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202411191155-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202512161740-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202512161740-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202512161740-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202512161740-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Substrate availability and citrate alter tca cycle metabolism and slc13a3 in macrophage immune responses".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202512161740-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Cell culture media are commonly formulated to enhance cell growth and often lack the physiological nutrient composition found in human blood plasma. The impact of substrate availability on immune cell metabolism and function remains incompletely understood. Here, we demonstrate that changes in culture medium composition affect mitochondrial metabolic pathways, immune responses, and transport in macrophages. Using mass spectrometry and stable isotope tracing, we identify citrate as a mediator linking extracellular substrate availability to intracellular metabolism. We also observe increased IL-6 secretion and elevated expression of plasma membrane transporter NaDC3 (SLC13A3) under physiological carbon source conditions that are reversed when citrate is excluded from the medium. Our findings demonstrate that extracellular substrate composition influences macrophage immunometabolism and identify citrate as an extracellular signal that modulates immune responses. This work highlights the importance of physiologically relevant nutrient availability in studying and targeting immunometabolic pathways.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202512161740-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202512161740-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202512161740-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202512161740-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202512161740-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202512161740-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202512161740-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202512161740-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202512161740-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-NC-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510270846-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510270846-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202510270846-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510270846-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Dataset on accentuated milled wax formwork for thin-shell robotic shotcreted architectural low-co2 concrete façade elements".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510270846-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset provides all additional data required to reproduce the experiments and verify the findings presented in the accompanying paper, “Accentuated Milled Wax Formwork for Thin Shell Robotic Shotcreted Architectural Low CO₂ Concrete Façade Elements.” The study introduces a novel digital fabrication process for producing waste-free wax formwork for architectural concrete applications within a closed-loop material system. It presents (a) a repeatable large-scale production method for wax blocks using an optimized single casting process; (b) four innovative, high-precision milling strategies incorporating accentuated surface patterns; (c) the investigation of coating systems to enhance concrete surface quality and facilitate demolding; and (d) the integration of robotic shotcreting with a low-CO₂ fine-grain concrete. The dataset includes the milling scripts, material product information and concrete mixture formulation organized in three-datasets that comprehensively document the investigations. These data support the reproducibility of the experimental procedures and the validation of the results described in the publication, particularly the fabrication of four fiber-reinforced, multi-curved thin-shell façade panels with parametric surface accentuations.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510270846-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510270846-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510270846-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2025"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510270846-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510270846-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202510270846-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510270846-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510270846-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510270846-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202504291413-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202504291413-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202504291413-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202504291413-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Experimental data from physical modeling of tsunami waves induced by subaerial granular landslides".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202504291413-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset provides the data of an experimental study to investigate the effect of grain size distribution, particle shape and surface roughness on landslide induced tsunami generation. Three types of material (granite chipping, river gravel and glass beads), four different grain sizes (d50 = 6 mm, 12 mm, 13 mm and 25 mm) and two slide masses (m_s = 5 kg and 10 kg) have been tested, resulting in 12 configurations of size, mass and material. Landslides were generated by releasing the material down a 30° slope into a flume filled with water. The dataset contains time series of water surface elevations and high-speed camera images tracking the slide movement.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202504291413-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202504291413-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202504291413-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202504291413-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202504291413-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202504291413-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202504291413-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202504291413-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202504291413-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160949-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160949-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202509160949-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160949-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Sluice and pumping station monitoring on the coast of lower saxony – knock".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160949-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Discharge data at the sluice and lock of sluice and pumpingstation Knock. Knock runs the inland drainage system of an area about 465 square kilometers near city of Emden. To model future impacts of climate change and create adaptation strategies of the drainage system, discharge data from the drainage Areas are crucial to calibrate and validate hydrological models. This Dataset can be used as a basis for hydrological modeling in the coastal Areas of lower saxony.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160949-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160949-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160949-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2025"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160949-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160949-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202509160949-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160949-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160949-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160949-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-SA-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601211621-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601211621-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202601211621-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601211621-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Point clouds of 147 trees in braunschweig, germany: terrestrial laser scans of free-standing acer pseudoplatanus, corylus colurna, ginkgo biloba, liquidambar styraciflua, ostrya carpinifolia, quercus robur, quercus robur ‘fastigiata,’ tilia cordata and tilia tomentosa".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601211621-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Between 2019 and 2025, 147 urban trees, belonging to nine species/cultivars were scanned with a terrestrial laser scanner. Sampling was carried out under leaf-off conditions on windless, dry winter days. One tree was scanned in summer, but was dead and had already lost all its leaves. Point clouds of the trees were obtained with the Riegl VZ400i terrestrial laser scanner. The scanner was positioned at least at four scan positions per tree to achieve full 360° coverage. The laser pulse repetition rate was set to 1200 kHz and the scan resolution to 20 millidegrees, which results in approximately one point per every 7 mm in 20 m distance from the scanner. The individual laser scans were registered and processed with the software RiSCAN PRO 2.18.1. Postprocessing included manually removing objects leaning at tree trunks (e.g., bikes) and filtering points with a high deviation (>=10) and low reflectance (-22). The density of the tree clouds was reduced to one point per cm³. Each tree was exported as a X,Y,Z point cloud. All but two specimens are on municipal land; the remaining two are on the campuses of Technische Universität Braunschweig and the Julius Kühn Institute. This dataset contains all point clouds and a table of geographic coordinates and scan dates.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601211621-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601211621-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601211621-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
