<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202606111316-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202606111316-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202606111316-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202606111316-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Calibrated time-varying path gain at 60 ghz and 300 ghz in the presence of human motion".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202606111316-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset contains time-resolved path gain measurements of line-of-sight (LOS) wireless communication links at 60 GHz and 300 GHz. The measurements capture the temporal evolution of the channel while a moving person intermittently obstructs the direct propagation path, causing shadowing and blockage effects. The recorded data provide insight into the dynamics of human-induced attenuation and channel variations in millimeter-wave and sub-THz frequency bands. These measurements can be used to analyze blockage characteristics, evaluate channel models, and support the design and performance assessment of future high-frequency wireless communication systems.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202606111316-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202606111316-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202606111316-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202606111316-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202606111316-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202606111316-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202606111316-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202606111316-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202606111316-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071130-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071130-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202510071130-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071130-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Geotechnical soil data for floating offshore wind applications: scottish, baltic and adriatic seas".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071130-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The design of resilient offshore structures requires knowledge of the geotechnical characteristics of soils present at a given location. In particular, seabed liquefaction, as one of the most severe forms of soil dynamics, must be well understood in order to prevent structural failure. Striving to gain such knowledge and insights, this dataset comprises the results of a unique, experimental campaign involving geotechnical characterisation of site-specific conditions for three selected locations (the Baltic Sea, the Scottish Sea, and the Adriatic Sea). For each of the above-mentioned regions, samples were collected from two locations. In total, preliminary tests were carried out for six types of soil. The geotechnical characterisation focused on determining soil susceptibility to liquefaction together with the mechanical properties of the tested sands, as well as supplementary key model parameters required for both experimental and numerical modelling. The experimental campaign began with a detailed microscopic examination and grain size distribution analysis to classify the soils. Based on the results, five of them were found to meet the initially adopted criteria (these are non-cohesive soils) and were subjected to a detailed testing procedure (a full set of monotonic and cyclic triaxial tests was performed). Soil samples marked with the symbol Adriatic 1 were identified as cohesive and therefore not suitable for liquefaction-related testing.The basic soil index properties were determined, such as grain size distribution, mean grain size d50, maximum and minimum void ratios, and hydraulic permeability. A series of advanced monotonic and cyclic triaxial tests was carried out using cyclic triaxial apparatus available at IBW PAN. Based on the results, the values of mechanical parameters (angle of internal friction, cohesion, elasticity constants) were determined. From the extensive series of monotonic and cyclic triaxial tests, the undrained and drained soil response was identified in order to define contractive and dilative regions. The liquefaction susceptibility of soils was also determined. A database of soil characteristics was compiled to support the development of surrogate soils with scaled properties for further use in physical and numerical modelling. Detailed results of the most significant tests performed are included in the appendixes attached to the report.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071130-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071130-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071130-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2025"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071130-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071130-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202510071130-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071130-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071130-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202510071130-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404230724-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404230724-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202404230724-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404230724-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Geometric and mechanical properties dataset of marram grass (calamagrostis arenaria, formerly ammophila arenaria) across dune habitats on spiekeroog island (december 2021 - december 2022): exploring seasonal and site-specific variability in marram grass\\' geometric and mechanical traits through field investigations and bending tests".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404230724-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset presents comprehensive geometric and mechanical attributes of Calamagrostis arenaria (formerly Ammophila arenaria), commonly known as marram grass, collected across diverse dune habitats on Spiekeroog Island from December 2021 to December 2022. The dataset includes field observations and three-point bending tests conducted on field samples, capturing seasonal variations and local disparities in plant morphology and mechanical properties. A novel categorization of marram grass based on its mechanical properties is introduced, resulting in the classification of sprout (sp), flowering stem (st), green (lg), and brown leaves (lb). The (bio)mechanical data in this dataset, obtained from bending tests, are presented as arithmetic means ± their standard deviations.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404230724-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404230724-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404230724-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2024"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404230724-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404230724-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202404230724-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404230724-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404230724-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202404230724-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-SA-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202604281426-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202604281426-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202604281426-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202604281426-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Analysis of simultaneous green roof co2 flux data measured with eddy covariance, automated chambers, and leaf chambers".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202604281426-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Urban green roofs have potential for local urban climate change mitigation, as they have been demonstrated to uptake CO2 from the atmosphere. However, most roofs are too small to qualify for area-integrating direct surface-atmosphere exchange measurements using the eddy covariance technique (EC), resulting in sparse data on net CO2 sequestration capacities. Small scale methods such as leaf chamber or automated surface chambers (AC) may provide a monitoring alternative for smaller roofs. To assess whether alternative methods can produce representative data on the CO2 sequestration capacity of an extensive green roof, simultaneous measurements at the scale of leaf, plants, and roof were conducted. The software provided includes the comparison of eddy covariance, automated chamber, and leaf chamber data with the respective code to replicate the images of the research article \\'Representativity of CO2 exchange on extensive green roofs: scaling from leaf to plant, and plant to roof scale\\'.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202604281426-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202604281426-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202604281426-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202604281426-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202604281426-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202604281426-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202604281426-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202604281426-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202604281426-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "MIT-License".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601071236-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601071236-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202601071236-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601071236-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Md_simulation_inputfiles".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601071236-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The molecular dynamics simulations were performed to investigate GGE as model compound for Lignin in different deep eutectic solvent - buffer solutions. This publication provides the input files for molecular dynamics simulations using GROMACS for the six different multi-component mixtures. The deep eutectic solvent is investigated with 2:1 and 4:1 EG:ChCl ratio in 12.5%, 25% and 50% DES:buffer solution. The buffer contains 0.4 mol glycine in water. Detailed information about the simulations and the evaluations are presented in the Paper: Efficient lignin dissolution and enzymatic depolymerization in ethylene glycol-based deep eutectic solvent mixtures: Integrated experimental and molecular dynamics study by Julian Schilke, Miriam Sprick, Gabriele Raabe and Anett Schallmey. The jupyter notebook calculates Kirkwood Buff Integrals based on radial distribution functions to gain insights into the affinities in the multi-component mixture of GGE in different DES-buffer solutions including the effect of the glycine buffer compound.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601071236-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601071236-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601071236-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601071236-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601071236-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202601071236-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601071236-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601071236-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202601071236-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-NC-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160932-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160932-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202509160932-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160932-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Sluice and pumping station monitoring on the coast of lower saxony – dangaster siel".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160932-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Discharge data at the sluice Dangaster Siel. Dangaster Siel runs the inland drainage system of an area about 329 square kilometers near city of Dangast. To model future impacts of climate change and create adaptation strategies of the drainage system, discharge data from the drainage Areas are crucial to calibrate and validate hydrological models. This Dataset can be used as a basis for hydrological modeling in the coastal Areas of lower saxony.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160932-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160932-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160932-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2025"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160932-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160932-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202509160932-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160932-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160932-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202509160932-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-SA-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151158-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151158-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202403151158-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151158-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Dataset for the study of frequency-domain model order reduction techniques in vibroacoustic applications".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151158-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The dataset is associated with the university dissertation titled \\'Surrogate modeling of high-dimensional vibroacoustic problems using parametric model order reduction\\' by Harikrishnan K. Sreekumar. Expensive direct numerical simulations are often used for vibroacoustic problems to yield insights about the model characteristics. These bottlenecks can be circumvented by generating a reduced order model that yields accurate system responses in real time. The current dataset includes various models that are used to investigate efficient reduction to approximate the frequency-domain response of the systems. Considered examples include (1) a simple plate model, (2) a generic aircraft fuselage model, and (3) a complex aircraft fuselage model for cabin noise assessments. The identified challenges of handling large-scale problems, frequency-dependent nature of the system entities and approaches to perform reduction for broadband applications are at focus. This current dataset publication contains essential artifacts (computational notebook, model data and primary results) that enable reproducibility of the outcome presented in the dissertation.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151158-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151158-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151158-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2024"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151158-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151158-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202403151158-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151158-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151158-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202403151158-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202503071410-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202503071410-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202503071410-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202503071410-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Bild- und videodaten zu versuchsreihe \\'verformung von flexiblem oberflächenendeffektor\\'".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202503071410-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The Dataset contains pictures and the corresponding video of experiments with a flexible trowel. The pictures are taken to verify the deformability of the developed trowel with and without lateral force - compensation. Without compensation the desired cubic spline shape was only observed for smaller deformations (>10mm per axis). With lateral compensation very good results were achieved (ca. +-70mm per axis).".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202503071410-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202503071410-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202503071410-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2025"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202503071410-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/leopard>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202503071410-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355/dbbs.084-202503071410-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202503071410-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202503071410-0.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202503071410-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "CC-BY-SA-4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605071224-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605071224-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202605071224-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605071224-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Data for the publication: a deep learning-based algorithm for spatiotemporal monitoring of debris in dam-break waves".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605071224-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "These data accompany the validation of the DeepRIS (Deep-learning Regression-based Identification and tracking of debriS) framework for automated debris detection and tracking in extreme flow conditions. The dataset originates from 91 medium-scale dam-break experiments conducted to investigate debris transport under varying hydrodynamic conditions, initial configurations, and material properties, including up to 240 debris elements per test. The experiments were performed to capture complex debris interactions, including entrainment, transport, clustering, and impact processes relevant to tsunami- and flash flood-like scenarios. Image sequences, ground-truth annotations, and processed trajectory data were generated using a hybrid YOLO–DeepSORT approach. These data support reproducibility of the associated study and provide a benchmark for the development and validation of multi-object tracking algorithms and optical monitoring techniques in hydraulic and coastal engineering. Please refer to the accompanying README file for detailed information on data structure, processing workflows, and usage guidelines. For further information, please contact t.hammer@tu-braunschweig.de.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605071224-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202605071224-0".
