<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506270810-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506270810-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.24355%2Fdbbs.084-202506270810-0>.
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506270810-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Sample intake port geometries for a light-duty diesel engine".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506270810-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "In Diesel engines, charge motion usually consists of swirl and squish flow patterns which are traditionally controlled through the design of the intake ports. A new fully parametric geometry was created and the simulational and experimental behavior when applied to a 2.0L VW light-duty Diesel engine is given in the conference entry \\'Simulation of Swirl and Discharge Coefficient Trade-off for Diesel Engine Intake Ports\\' to 17th International Conference on Engines & Vehicles for Sustainable Transport, Capri, Italy. Some of the intake ports with different parameters can be found in this repository.".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506270810-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506270810-0".
<http://localhost:5002/leo-doi-10-24355-dbbs-084-202506270810-0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2025"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
